  "result": "Perfect! All 231 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statements:\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Created `src/statements.js`** with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function:\n   - Validates customer exists using normalized ID (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if not found)\n   - Filters invoices by:\n     - Customer ID (after normalizing both customer ID and invoice customerId)\n     - Status: only 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n     - Issue date: on or before asOf date\n   - Maps each invoice to: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n   - Sorts results by issueDate (ascending)\n   - Calculates `totalDue` as sum of all due amounts\n   - Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n\n2. **Fixed `issueInvoice()` function** in src/invoices.js:\n   - Now preserves `terms` and `dueDate` properties from draft invoices\n   - Ensures complete invoice data flows through the issuance process\n\n3. **Added 16 comprehensive tests**:\n   - Empty statement for customer\n   - Single and multiple invoices\n   - Filtering by status (excludes draft and paid invoices)\n   - Filtering by date (excludes future-dated invoices)\n   - Sorting by issueDate\n   - Total due calculation\n   - Partially paid invoices\n   - Mixed customer invoices\n   - ID normalization (mixed case, spaces)\n   - Invoice format validation\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- Customer IDs normalized consistently (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed)\n- Only issued/partially_paid invoices included in statement\n- Invoices sorted chronologically by issue date\n- Due amounts calculated using `balanceDue()` from payments module\n- Complete invoice data (including dueDate from terms) preserved through issuance\n\nAll 231 tests pass \u2713",
